TI  - An Intelligent Cognitive Framework Integrating SOAR Architecture with Large Language Models and AI Agents for Cyber Defence
PY  - 2025
T2  - 2025 IEEE 1st International Conference on Recent Trends in Computing and Smart Mobility, RCSM 2025
DO  - 10.1109/RCSM67767.2025.11506691
UR  - https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/105041537566?origin=resultslist
AB  - The increasing sophistication of cyber adversaries calls for a shift in security operations from a reactive to a proactive approach in enterprise security architectures. A self-sufficient cyber defence concept based on an AI-powered SOAR (Security Orchestration, Automation, and Response) system is presented here. The proposed system features intelligent agents and machine-learning-driven threat-assessment to enable alarm triage, correlation, and incident response in real time. By injecting Large Language Models (LLMs) for contextualized reasoning and decision support, the system enhances detection accuracy, reduces human intervention, and accelerates response efficiency. The AI-driven SOAR system experimental results show that the framework significantly improves tactical agility as well as dynamic defence against evolving cyberthreats. Moreover, the model's ability to perform adaptive learning allows it to keep learning from historical incidents, thus, it can continuously resist novel threats. The AI-SOAR solution speeds up incident response and recovery times while lowering false positives by implementing context-aware reasoning. In comparison to traditional rule-based SOAR systems, study results employing baseline intrusion detection datasets like CICIDS-2017 show enhanced detection accuracy, efficiency in operation, and scalability. Thus, the suggested AI-SOAR framework offers a self-learning, intelligent, and transparent approach to contemporary cyber threat management, filling the gap across automated and autonomous in cyberspace. © 2025 IEEE.
