TI  - Ai SecureDataGuard: A Big Data Security, Privacy-Preserving and Visualization System for LLM-Powered Smart Homes
PY  - 2026
T2  - Proceedings - 2026 IEEE 3rd International Conference on Big Data Science and Engineering, ICBDSE 2026
DO  - 10.1109/ICBDSE70225.2026.11635380
UR  - https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/105048853086?origin=resultslist
AB  - Now large language models and that multi-agent frameworks are widely used, platforms like MOSS can let users talk to smart homes naturally and link up all kinds of household devices. But there's a slew of tough issues hindering these products from practical commercial application IoT data from every device, constant user privacy leaks, intentional prompt injection and safety guardrail evasion attacks, plus no tool to monitor all risks instantly.For the resolution of all aforementioned drawbacks, I built a complete big data security framework named SecureDataGuard. It packs malicious input screening, differential privacy, federated lightweight anomaly tracking and real-time data visual monitoring into one set of tools. I built the whole system on top of MOSS AI's multi-agent structure, and also adopted mature industrial AI security tools from Anquan Data Intelligence.First, I made a two-step intent recognition algorithm to block prompt injection and jailbreak attempts. Second, I put together a mixed privacy protection scheme, so we can use data normally without exposing raw user information. I also developed a slimmed-down Transformer model called LADT to catch abnormal device behaviors the second they happen. On top of that, I built a monitoring panel with StarRocks and ECharts, so administrators can track every risk across bird's-eye view of the whole system.A large set of empirical experiments was implemented with real-world smart home operation records to corroborate the system's performance.. Encouraging results are observed in our experiments. The system accurately recognizes user commands with an accuracy rate of 97.8%.Identifies anomalous activity within 18 ms and lowers privacy leakage probability by 92%. All 18 key security metrics on the dashboard update within milliseconds. This work delivers a practical, deployable technical solution to handle smart home data safety, privacy risks, Anomalous Event Detection and Visual Risk Control © 2026 IEEE.
