TI  - AI Agent-Assisted Lightweight Intrusion Detection for IoT Devices
PY  - 2026
T2  - ICHORA 2026 - 8th International Congress on Human-Computer Interaction, Optimization and Robotic Applications, Proceedings
DO  - 10.1109/ICHORA69329.2026.11537202
UR  - https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/105042119987?origin=resultslist
AB  - The rapid increase in Internet of Things (IoT) devices has raised serious security concerns, mainly due to growing traffic volumes and more complex cyber threats. At the same time, many existing intrusion detection systems (IDS) are not well suited for resource-constrained edge environments. In this study, a lightweight IDS framework supported by an Artificial Intelligence (AI) agent is introduced for such settings. The system is built around a compact 1D-ResNet model with 28,759 parameters (approximately $\mathbf{1 2 7 K B}$), allowing multiclass attack detection with low computational cost. Rather than focusing only on accuracy, the model is designed to operate as a fast pre-filter. It scans network traffic and identifies suspicious flows at an early stage, so that more detailed analysis can be handled by more complex models. This method is scalable and supports layered IDS designs. Proposed model trained on the CIC-IoT-2023 dataset, which has a significant class imbalance. To overcome this imbalance problem, the Synthetic Minority Over-sampling Technique (SMOTE) was applied to improve the detection of minority attack types. In addition, a cloud-based AI Security Analyst agent powered by Gemini 2.5 Flash converts model outputs and metadata into structured, human-readable reports. Lightweight 1D-ResNet model performed 82.84% accuracy, while keeping computational overhead low. These results demonstrate that the proposed approach is suitable for real-time edge deployment.  © 2026 IEEE.
