AB  - To counter sophisticated social engineering attacks, traditional email filters often fail to detect novel phishing threats due to insufficient contextual understanding. This paper proposes MRE-Guard, a dual-agent collaborative detection framework. It introduces an interaction mechanism between a Retrieval Agent, which provides reliable external knowledge via a balanced retrieval strategy, and a QA Agent, which performs final decisionmaking through chain-of-thought reasoning. Experiments on a self-constructed comprehensive email dataset show that MREGuard, powered by DeepSeek, achieves an F1-score of 88.89% and an accuracy of 89.17%, outperforming zero-shot baselines by 26.49%. The results demonstrate that the synergy between retrieval and reasoning significantly enhances threat detection and interpretability in dynamic email environments.  © 2026 IEEE.
