AB  - Large Language Model (LLM) agents are increasingly integrated into Security Operations Centers (SOCs) to automate alert analysis and incident response, potentially enhancing capabilities while reducing effort. However, they may produce inconsistent, unpredictable, and misaligned recommendations, compromising reliability and accountability. We propose a framework combining deterministic and agent-driven processes to achieve reliability, accountability, and flexibility. As an initial case study, we implement this framework in an emulated Security Information and Event Management (SIEM) environment, which prepares the ground for future systematic evaluation of reliable LLM-Assisted SOC operations.  © 2026 Copyright held by the owner/author(s).
