AB  - A reliable network solution is needed due to the rapid growth of autonomous vehicles and Intelligent Transportation Systems (ITS). So, we developed a new Generative Artificial Intelligence (GenAI) Guided Cyber Attack Detection and Classification in Autonomous Intelligent Cars (GAICAD) model meets these needs by integrating advanced deep learning, path planning, and GenAI-based cybersecurity within Vehicle Ad Hoc Networks (VANETs). GAICAD uses a hybrid deep learning technique combining CNNs and DBNs to better categorize and predict driving conditions, improving network security and vehicle communication. The A∗ path planning method to find optimal routes amid varying traffic. GenAI-driven cybersecurity also detects threats and anomalies in real-time. Simulation results show GAICAD with previous models, achieving a 96% data delivery rate and a minimal data leak rate of 2%. It maintains effective communication with an average delay of 320 ms, even in heavy traffic. GAICAD improves traffic management, cybersecurity, and real-time decision-making, supporting the development of safer autonomous vehicle systems in smart cities.  © 2025 IEEE.
