TI  - Examining the Factors Influencing Generative AI's Impact on Quantum Cybersecurity: A Thematic Analysis
PY  - 2025
T2  - Proceedings of IEEE International Conference on Modelling, Simulation and Intelligent Computing, MoSICom 2025
SP  - 518
EP  - 524
DO  - 10.1109/MoSICom67153.2025.11398253
UR  - https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/105036344302?origin=resultslist
AB  - The rapid advancement of generative AI and its integration with quantum cybersecurity present significant opportunities and new problems. While generative AI can improve security in quantum computing, it also brings new risks and uncertainties. Discovering the driving forces or constraints of using generative A I in this application domain is essential to devising effective mechanisms for harnessing its possibilities while minimizing the risks. The main objectives of this paper are to perform a thematic analysis on several primary motivators and demotivators driving the adoption and impact of generative AI in quantum cybersecurity. The study found several key motivators, such as the potential for new predictive capabilities, the automation of threat detection, and the strengthening of quantum encryption protocols. The sources of demotivation included suspicion about the dependability of AI models in a super complex quantum world, ethical problems of the autonomous decision-making AI, and node computational power to integrate AI into quantum. These actors are identified to play an essential role in the feasibility and acceptability of generative AI for quantum cybersecurity.  © 2025 IEEE.
