AB  - Converging IoT and Artificial Intelligence (AI) drives the transition to cognitive smart environments. However, current cloud-centric solutions introduce critical privacy, latency, and reliability vulnerabilities. This paper presents the design of a decentralized smart home system based on Edge Computing. The proposed architecture utilizes a Raspberry Pi 4 as a central Cognitive Hub, integrating a hybrid Generative AI agent (LLM). While local STT (Vosk) ensures initial audio processing to maintain voice privacy, the Gemini API is integrated to provide advanced semantic reasoning on the resulting text. This enables the system to move beyond rigid, keyword-based commands towards natural language understanding, where complex user intents are dynamically mapped to specific IoT control payloads. Unlike traditional rigid command systems, this agent semantically interprets natural language inputs and dynamically generates complex JSON control payloads for the distributed ESP32 microcontrollers via MQTT. A key contribution is the implementation of a real-time solar tracking and weather-adaptive control for energy optimization, which augments a local Proportional controller with external meteorological data to preemptively adjust system behavior during adverse weather. Furthermore, the system integrates local Artificial Intelligence (AI) for biometric security and context-aware safety protocols, enabling rapid, autonomous response to hazards like gas leaks without cloud reliance. Preliminary results demonstrate that this modular architecture offers a scalable, low-cost, and privacy-centric alternative to proprietary ecosystem.  © 2026 IEEE.
