TI  - Agentic SOC: A Hierarchical Swarm-Orchestrated Multi-Agent LLM Architecture for Autonomous OT Cyber Defense
PY  - 2026
T2  - 2026 International Wireless Communications and Mobile Computing Conference, IWCMC 2026
SP  - 1379
EP  - 1384
DO  - 10.1109/IWCMC69287.2026.11579813
UR  - https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/105044707023?origin=resultslist
AB  - The convergence of enterprise IT networks with operational technology (OT), industrial control systems (ICS), and 5G/6G wireless-enabled cyber-physical infrastructures has expanded the attack surface of critical environments, exposing limitations in traditional IT-centric Security Operations Centers (SOCs). IT-OT systems impose strict latency, safety, and availability constraints, while rule-based detection and human-driven triage lead to alert fatigue, delayed response, and fragmented visibility across wired and wireless domains. This paper presents Agentic SOC, a hierarchical swarm-orchestrated multi-agent LLM architecture for autonomous and adaptive cyber defense in IT-OT converged networks. The architecture decomposes SOC operations into three cooperative tiers: a perception layer of distributed agents performing real-time telemetry analysis across IT, OT, and wireless network domains; a reasoning layer executing cross-domain correlation, MITRE ATT&CK (including ICS) mapping, and coordinated mitigation; and a strategic leader agent conducting kill-chain reconstruction, RAG-grounded threat hunting, and adversarial simulation. We implement and evaluate Agentic SOC under a managed security service provider (MSSP) model across four safety-critical scenarios: 6G telecom infrastructure, a power generation plant, a railway control system, and a three-dimensional Security of Air-Ground-Space Integrated Networks (SAGIN) environment. Experimental benchmarking demonstrates broader threat coverage, improved cross-domain correlation, reduced false positives, and a lower mean time to detection and response compared to flat, multi-agent, and rule-based SOC baselines while preserving human-in-the-loop governance. Agentic SOC provides an experimentally validated blueprint for AI-native, self-protecting SOC architectures in next-generation IT-OT cyber-physical systems. © 2026 IEEE.
