EP  - 396
DO  - 10.1109/ICBASE70763.2026.11619482
UR  - https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/105047076315?origin=resultslist
AB  - To mitigate alert fatigue caused by highly obfuscated attacks in Web log anomaly detection, and to overcome the cognitive overload and conservative bias of standalone Large Language Models (LLMs) when processing conflicting evidence, this paper proposes an anomaly detection architecture integrating heterogeneous retrieval augmentation and multi-agent games (Multi-Agent RAG). This architecture constructs a heterogeneous dual-track knowledge retrieval mechanism, physically isolating conflicting knowledge via vector-based fuzzy semantic retrieval and hash-based precise matching to decouple the extraction of external intelligence and local profiles. On this basis, a red-blue multi-agent adversarial debate executes bidirectional logical cross-examinations, mapping fuzzy log semantics into deterministic security features. Finally, a judge agent executes adaptive routing and dynamic arbitration. Experiments on the AIT-LDS dataset show that the proposed method achieves 97.30% accuracy and 99.58% precision, while the generated white-box diagnostic reports significantly enhance the explainability of audit results. © 2026 IEEE.
