TI  - Autonomous AI Agents for Offensive Security: Redefining Penetration Testing and Remediation
PY  - 2025
T2  - ICRTEECT 2025 - 2nd International Conference on Recent Trends in Electrical, Electronics and Computing Technologies
DO  - 10.1109/ICRTEECT67512.2025.11448772
UR  - https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/105037335571?origin=resultslist
AB  - The AI-Driven Paradigm Shift in Offensive Security. The integration of Artificial Intelligence (AI) into cybersecurity operations marks a fundamental shift, particularly in the domain of offensive security and penetration testing. Autonomous AI agents, powered by advanced machine learning and Large Language Models (LLMs), are now capable of executing the full spectrum of offensive operations: from reconnaissance and vulnerability enumeration to exploitation and post-exploitation. These agents operate with minimal human oversight, enabling rapid, adaptive, and context-aware decision-making across dynamically shifting environments.Such a transformation speeds the penetrating testing process that previously required weeks and now takes only hours but is vastly more in-depth and thorough as well. Since ephemeral workloads (such as on the cloud, or as reached by CI/CD pipelines), and distributed attack surfaces are multiplying, the resiliency and speed of AI-based systems will be essential. Even human roles will change accordingly, shifting the operating KPIs of ensuring correct manual execution to strategic decision-making to risk, ethics, and action, such as the Mean Time to Remediate (MTTR) and to Respond (MTTR).In this age of an average data breach cost of more than 4.45 million dollars, AI is shifting not only to a strategic advantage but also to a minimum requirement. Companies which do not automate AI in offensive security may be left surpassed by opponents who already have access to automated power. The ones that survive will restructure the future of thunderous, adaptive cyber defense. © 2025 IEEE.
