UR  - https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/105018039270?origin=resultslist
AB  - In the context of the continuous evolution of the industrial internet, cybersecurity ranges play a crucial role in supporting the design and verification of industrial system protection mechanisms. Addressing the limitations of existing ranges in terms of construction complexity, traffic authenticity, and attack adaptability, this paper proposes the Large-language-model Assisted Security Range (LASR) framework. This framework combines the semantic modeling capabilities of large language models, hypergraph-driven network topology generation mechanisms, traffic synthesis methods using generative adversarial networks, and multi-agent collaboration mechanisms to build an intelligent simulation system with high scalability and adaptability. Each agent collaborates in attack modeling, intelligence analysis, defense response, and strategy optimization, achieving full-process modeling and strategy evolution of dynamic attack-defense processes. Taking the nuclear power industry as an example, this paper explores the application potential of this framework in complex industrial control systems, providing low-cost, high-performance theoretical support and system references for industrial cybersecurity research and protection technology verification. © 2025 World Scientific Publishing Company.
