DO  - 10.1109/NetSoft70012.2026.11603421
UR  - https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/105045842299?origin=resultslist
AB  - The dynamic and heterogeneous nature of 5G and beyond (B5G) networks creates fertile ground for sophisticated Zero-Day attacks that evade traditional, signature-based defences. This paper presents a novel approach that utilizes a bifurcated, hybrid neuro-symbolic framework - conceptually aligned with dual-process cognitive theory - for autonomous intrusion detection and mitigation from context-rich flow telemetry. By deploying a computationally asymmetric pipeline, our method avoids reliance on monolithic deep learning architectures and uses a high-speed, confidence-gated XGBoost classifier (System 1) to evaluate traffic at wirespeed and instantly discover anomalous deviations. Evaluations demonstrate strong performance in managing out-of-distribution traffic and detecting previously unknown threats, offering a scalable, highly reliable, and interpretable solution for next-generation network security. The tactical mechanism is dynamically linked to a Retrieval-Augmented Large Language Model (System 2) that provides deep semantic reasoning concerning ambiguous anomalies and synthesizes highly targeted JSON mitigation payloads, which are strictly bounded by deterministic mathematical guardrails to suppress AI hallucination. © 2026 IEEE.
